## Root causes found (previous status was a misdiagnosis)

The earlier note claimed the game "stalls after Instance_LoadContent" and
suggested a real display, SDL videodriver changes, or manual interaction. The
full SMAPI log disproved that:

1. **Save folder / inner file name mismatch.** The isolated save was
   `Saves/farm-year1-day5/`, but the main save file inside it was
   `Agroeco_421179919`. Stardew resolves a save as `Saves/<name>/<name>`, so
   `SaveGame.Load("farm-year1-day5")` logged `DebugOutput: File does not exist`
   and returned to the title screen. The game kept running and rendering; it
   never stalled. Fixed in `scripts/lib/save.sh` (`save_align_inner_name`), and
   `save_prepare` now fails loudly (19) when the working copy has no
   `<name>/<name>` file.
2. **The bundle kept only a grep-filtered log.** `signals_smapi_log_excerpt`
   kept only `elapsed`, `DayEnding`/`SoilGrowthModifierCompleted`, and
   `not main player` lines, so `artifacts/smapi-log.txt` was two lines long and
   looked like a five-second stall. It now copies the full SMAPI log.

The spec 010 `fixtures/valid/*.scenario.json` files are schema contract
fixtures, not runnable gameplay scenarios (off-map tile `-10,5`, no macro
files). T137 uses the real scenario at
`specs/004-playable-compost-loop/scenarios/compost-growth-hardening.scenario.json`.

